{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>If Elohim will be with me</b> — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 28:20): if He keeps for me these promises that He promised me. And the reason for the condition is that sin should not intervene. And thus they said in Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 76:2), Rav Huna in the name of Rabbi Acha: it is written \"Behold, I am with you\" and it is written \"If Elohim will be with me\" — rather, from here we learn that there is no guarantee for the righteous in this world. And it is further possible, according to the plain sense, that there is no doubt in the matter at all, but regarding all future events Scripture says \"if,\" as in \"until if I have done,\" and likewise \"and if the Jubilee should come to the children of Israel\" (Numbers 36:4) — if the time comes that the condition materializes, then the event will be fulfilled, that is to say, when it arrives:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:20.410909906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}